  <result aggregation-status="1" type="1">
   <title>
    <narrative xml:lang="EN">Annual Output Results</narrative>
   </title>
   <indicator ascending="0" measure="5">
    <title>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Output Indicator</narrative>
    </title>
    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Number of the policy framework strengthened to support a sustainable charcoal value chain in Angola;
2. Number of the benefits of sustainable charcoal production technology, briquetting and energy-efficient charcoal stoves accepted by producers and peri-urban consumers;
3. Number of Institutional and human capacities for sustainable charcoal production and utilization strengthened through partnerships for knowledge transfer and professional training;
4. Percentage of the Monitoring &amp; Evaluation plan for the Project implemented.</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2016">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Policies, regulation and institutions are not geared for effective intervention in the charcoal sector
2. Traditional charcoal production relies on a combination of rudimentary technology, involving virtually zero capital investment, and basic operator skills
3. The institutional and human capacities for the production and use of sustainable charcoal are very weak or nonexistent
4. Need to implement the monitoring and evaluation plan for the project.</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2020-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2020-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Implement quarterly field visits to the communities part of the project activities;
2. Implement south-south exchange with Zambia;
3. Implement activities for young people in the production and marketing of sustainable cookstoves;
4. Produce charcoal white book;
5. Produce national charcoal strategy
6. Integrate COVID awareness and information into ongoing outreach activities at no extra cost to project.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1) Field visits to the comunities by the project coordination team based in Luanda were not posible due to covid 19 pandemic travel restrictions. However, the implemented partners placed their project officers ate the community level during the pandemic to provide better support to the communities.
2) It was not posible to do the South-south exchange with zambia, However in the firts quarter of 2020 project staff were to attend and participate in a workshop in Lusaka related to sustainable charcoal 
3) Activities were implemented by ADPP and Don Bosco related to the production and promotion of eficient cooking stoves deigned by the University of Cordova with funds from the project.
4-5) The TOR for the white book and the charcoal strategy were prepared with IDF and DNAAC, however their publication was not yet done due to goverment restructuration process (3 diferent ministers of environment in the year) and not clear delegation of authority to aprove new project activities and make payments.
6) Integrated Covid awareness and information was done by the implementing partners (ADPP, COSPE, Don Bosco, UJES) during the implementation of activities at no extra cost. 
5)</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Produce charcoal white book and national charcoal strategy
2. Integrate Covid19 awareness and information into ongoing outreach activities at no extra cost to project.
3. Support the Angolan government in its strategic work related to climate change and emission reductions related to deforestation. Support in development and submission of NDCs. 
4.Build new partnerships with INAPEM and INAFOP to promote business incubators
5.Continue raising awareness on sustainable options of the charcoal sector both in rural and urban areas, as well as focus on finding ways to enhance continuity of the project once the various activities end</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Procurement process ongoing, ToRs approved by the ministry (MCTA) and the request for tenders have been advertised twice. However, there has been a too low number of tenders and consultants for implementation are not found yet.
2. Information and awareness of rules and precautions have been integrated into outgoing outreach activities in communities and at the schools with training activities.
3. The project have supported the government with the development of their Nationally determined contributions (NDCs) and a draft have been submitted.
4. The partnerships with INAPEM and INAFOP have been strengthened over the year and the detailed for the training activities have been outlined for implementation starting in the beginning of 2022.
5. The project partners have actively been working in over 20 communities in Cuanza Sul and Huambo and at several educational centers with awareness raising on sustainable options of the charcoal sector both in rural and urban areas. The activities have been reaching a wide range of people, from children to the traditional leaders of the communities. The knowledge level is higher and the people that have been trained now understand better the benefits and necessity of keeping the charcoal production methods sustainable and how this effects them on a personal level.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">1. Produce charcoal white book and national charcoal strategy
2. Support the Angolan government in its strategic work related to climate change and emission reductions related to deforestation.
3.Build new partnerships with INAPEM and INAFOP to increase the number of people being trained and to promote business incubators
4.Continue raising awareness on sustainable options of the charcoal sector both in rural and urban areas, as well as focus on finding ways to enhance continuity of the project once the various activities end.
5. Organize an international conference on sustainable charcoal 
6. Design a certification scheme for sustainable charcoal and support the communities in the project to get licensing for their charcoal through IDF
7. Seek extension for the project and if not granted; make the final evaluation and finalize the project</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
    </period>
   </indicator>
